[client] Step 1: asking the portmapper (port 9111) where program 0x20001, version 1 lives...
[client]         portmapper says: port 49269

[client] Step 2: connecting DIRECTLY to port 49269 (no portmapper involved this time)
[client]         ADD(3, 4) = 7

[client] ---- Now: a real multi-fragment record-marking test ----
[client] Sending ONE logical RPC call, split across TWO TCP-level
[client] fragments, each with its own record-marking header,
[client] exactly as RFC 5531 section 11 allows.

[client] Fragment 1 header bytes: 00 00 00 10  (top bit = 0 -> more fragments follow; length = 16)
[client] Fragment 2 header bytes: 80 00 00 10  (top bit = 1 -> LAST fragment; length = 16)
[client] Server correctly reassembled both fragments and replied: 111 + 222 = 333
